# Eclipsed Steppe: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls a Plains (one
# basic) and a Scrubland (the Plains and Swamp types, but not basic, CR 205.4a): one basic is below the two, so its
# Eclipsed Steppe enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with a Plains and a
# Swamp of its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Scrubland
Eclipsed Steppe
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Swamp
Eclipsed Steppe
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Scrubland.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Eclipsed Steppe.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Eclipsed Steppe.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Eclipsed Steppe.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Eclipsed Steppe.Tapped = false
